# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# The operational-test Dockerfiles (scripts/operational/*) use `COPY . .` to
# build the harness examples from source. Without this file the context
# includes the ~32G `target/` dir and the whole of it is sent to the daemon
# before the build starts. Keep the context to source only.

# Build artefacts (the big one)
target/
**/target/

# VCS + history
.git/
.gitignore

# Docs, specs, plans (not needed to compile the harness). README/licence at
# root are KB-sized and may be referenced by Cargo.toml, so leave them.
docs/

# Local secrets -- never let these land in a builder layer
.env
.env.*

# Local dev / agent artefacts. benches/ stays in the context: Cargo.toml
# declares seven [[bench]] targets, and cargo refuses to parse the manifest
# when their files are missing, so excluding them breaks every image build.
.claude/
.codex/
.cursor/
.gemini/
.mcp.json
.ai-version

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
**/*.swp
.DS_Store
